# EMZI Nexus — finish checklist

When completing **any** task that touches UI, API, auth, integrations, or deployment, verify against `docs/README.md` before saying the work is done.

## Always read first

- Index: `docs/README.md`
- UI/UX: `docs/DESIGN_TEMPLATE.md` (pass §28 pre-ship for UI work)

## Integration docs — read before finishing

| If you touched… | Read this spec |
|-----------------|----------------|
| `*Webhook*`, `NotificationSettings`, `event_webhook`, notification triggers | `docs/event-webhook-setup.md` §2 + §4.1 |
| SSO, `SsoController`, `NexusSsoSettings`, `nexus_sso_id` | `docs/nexus-sso-setup.md` |
| `routes/api.php` under `mcp/v1`, MCP controllers | `docs/emzi-nexus-mcp-catalog-spec.md` |

Also apply `.cursor/rules/event-webhook-emitter.mdc` when editing webhook-related files.

## Before marking complete

**Frontend / UI** (`frontend/src/**`):

- [ ] Semantic tokens only (`bg-card`, `text-foreground`) — no raw `slate-*` / `bg-white` on app pages
- [ ] shadcn/ui + Lucide; page title + description pattern (DESIGN_TEMPLATE §4.3)
- [ ] Back actions use `useGoBack` / `BackButton`, not hardcoded back links (§7.5)
- [ ] User decisions use `ConfirmDialog` before persist/delete/mode switch (§11.3)
- [ ] Mobile dialogs: `w-[calc(100vw-1.5rem)]`, horizontal footer on mobile (§11.9)
- [ ] Glass dock matches `docs/MOBILE_BOTTOM_NAV_DESIGN.md` if nav changed

**Backend / DB**:

- [ ] Integer PKs on app tables — no UUID primary keys (`docs/INITIAL_SETUP.md`)
- [ ] SSO changes match `docs/nexus-sso-setup.md`
- [ ] MCP routes under `/api/mcp/v1/` per `docs/emzi-nexus-mcp-catalog-spec.md`

**Event webhooks (emitter)** — when changing delivery, settings, or notification triggers:

Read `docs/event-webhook-setup.md` §2 and §4.1. Verify:

- [ ] Config: multiple webhooks per installation; each with `id` (webhook_id), `url`, `secret` (`whsec_`, ≥32 chars), `enabled`, per-event `events` map
- [ ] Payload top-level: `event`, `timestamp`, `webhook_id`, `type`, `category`, `title`, `body`, `action_url`, `nexus_sso_id` (not internal user IDs)
- [ ] Nested object key = event domain prefix (`domain`, `alert`, `user`, …)
- [ ] Recipients: resolve `users.nexus_sso_id`; one POST per distinct ID; dedupe; `null` if unlinked
- [ ] HTTP: POST JSON, `X-Webhook-Secret`, `User-Agent: Sentinel-Webhooks/1.0`, 10s timeout, fire-and-forget (failures logged, never block main request)
- [ ] `action_url` built from `FRONTEND_URL` / `config('sentinel.frontend_url')`
- [ ] Test delivery: `webhook.test` via `POST /api/settings/event-webhook/test` + Settings → Notifications “Send test”
- [ ] New events: `{domain}.{action}` naming, metadata (`type`/`category`), trigger wired, toggles in `WEBHOOK_EVENT_OPTIONS` + `SettingsService::EVENT_WEBHOOK_KEYS`

**Sentinel webhook reference files:**

- `backend/app/Services/EventWebhookService.php`
- `backend/app/Services/LinkWebhookService.php`
- `backend/app/Support/EventWebhookMetadata.php`
- `backend/app/Services/SettingsService.php` (`event_webhook`)
- `frontend/src/components/settings/NotificationSettings.jsx`

**Deploy / env**:

- [ ] Split domains: `VITE_API_BASE_URL` points to API host (`docs/REACT_SPA_APACHE_HTACCESS.md`)

## Report format

If checks apply, end with a short **Compliance** note: what was verified or what still needs manual QA. Skip if the change was docs-only or unrelated (e.g. typo in a comment).
